115:export class PostFX {

Signal/reboot works. But `#cam-signal-val` text for reboot only updates if cam open; after closing no need. HUD signal bar will show low/recharging.

One issue: when camSignal lost, `game.camOffline` stays true until `rebootCams` resets. After 6s auto reboot, `camOffline` remains true (only rebootCams sets false). `_updateSignal` doesn't reset camOffline. Then feed overlay `setFeedClock` shows "NO SIGNAL" if camOffline; and updateCamHud shows SIGNAL LOST. But feed itself renders fine. After auto-reboot (camRebootT reaches 0), should set camOffline=false. Currently in game.update:
```
if (this.camRebootT > 0) {
  this.camRebootT = max(0, ...);
  if (this.camRebootT === 0) { this.camSignal=100; onMessage('Cameras back online.'); }
}
```
But `this.camOffline` not reset. Fix in game.js: set `this.camOffline = false;` there. Also `_updateSignal` set `camOffline=true`. Good.

Patch.

